DS ENCHANTING: export the live enchanting state and expose command bridges so the companion can
replace the native EnchantingDialog, which windowmanagerimp already suppresses when the
"game_ui_enchanting" element is DS (companion-hide-gamewindows-on-dsmode.patch — the gate was wired
dormant long before this patch existed).

PRESENTATION + INPUT FORWARDING ONLY. MWMechanics::Enchanting keeps every rule: the cast-style state
machine (nextCastStyle's per-item-class table), the ACCUMULATING per-effect cost, the enchant-points
capacity check, the price / charge / success-chance formulas, the self-enchant roll and the soul-gem
consumption that happens whatever the outcome. EffectEditorBase keeps the effect list, the 8-effect
cap, the non-uniform duplicate rule and the add-then-remove-on-cancel semantics.

Five things are load-bearing:

  * THE FOUR WindowModals NEEDED THEIR OWN GATES. windowmanagerimp's GM_Enchanting suppression only
    hides mGuiModeStates[GM_Enchanting].mWindows — it does NOT reach EditEffectDialog (a member of
    EffectEditorBase), ItemSelectionDialog (created on demand), SelectSkillDialog or
    SelectAttributeDialog, all of which are shown independently via setVisible(true). Without the
    gates added here they would pop up ALONE on the TOP screen in DS mode — the same class of
    problem as the Persuasion modal. The EffectEditorBase gate tests mType as well as the element,
    because SpellCreationDialog shares that base and is still Vanilla-only.

  * THE CLOSE SIGNAL IS EMITTED EXPLICITLY from exit(), onCancelButtonClicked, onReferenceUnavailable
    and both removeGuiMode paths inside onBuyButtonClicked. In DS mode the window is hidden, so
    WindowBase::setVisible() produces no visible->hidden edge and the ordinary onClose() never runs
    on the real mode-pop. onClose() is still overridden (with the usual !containsMode guard, which
    also suppresses the spurious emit the DS suppression's own transient hide would produce) to
    cover Vanilla mode. All paths funnel through the once-guarded companionEmitClosed().

  * THE STATE BATCH IS EMITTED FROM THE TAIL OF updateLabels(), which is the one hook EVERY mutation
    path reaches: setPtr, item/soul select and clear, onTypeButtonClicked, and notifyEffectsChanged
    — which updateEffectsView calls after every effect add / modify / remove. STREAMED one small
    line per record: the two picker lists are bounded only by how much the player is carrying, so a
    single line would hit the 4096-byte stdout-flush truncation.

  * THE EFFECT DISPLAY LINE IS COMPOSED IN C++ (companionEnchantEffectLine), a faithful
    transcription of Widgets::MWSpellEffect::updateWidgets — getMagicEffectString plus a
    magnitude-display-type switch and eleven GMSTs. It lives beside the original so the DS readout
    cannot drift from the wording vanilla shows on the top screen. The only difference is that the
    "#{sin}"/"#{sfootarea}" tags vanilla leaves for setCaptionWithReplacing are resolved here.

  * RAW FLAG WORDS ARE EXPORTED, NOT PRECOMPUTED BOOLEANS. Which range options and which sliders are
    legal depends on the LIVE cast style as well as the effect record (Constant Effect force-allows
    Self, force-denies Touch/Target and hides Duration), and the player changes that with the Type
    button while the browse list stands still — so the DS side must recompute the same way the
    engine does rather than cache an answer.

ONE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE, requested and confirmed, and it is deliberately NARROW:
companionInitialRange reproduces vanilla's real two-step behaviour (newEffect's cascade, then the
unconditional onRangeButtonClicked that advances once and re-checks) for EVERY availability
combination, with a single exception — an effect allowing Touch and Target but NOT Self opens on
Touch instead of vanilla's Target. That combination is the reported bug: the cascade leaves Touch
and the unconditional advance steps straight past it. Every other combination matches vanilla
exactly, including the Touch-only case where vanilla itself lands on an ILLEGAL Self (documented at
the function; the DS editor's own legality guard corrects it on open, so no second exception is
hard-coded here). A separate companionFirstLegalRange handles the different question of repairing an
out-of-range _effect_set. Everything else about the editor is vanilla's, including the fixed slider bounds
(Magnitude 1..100, Duration 1..1440, Area 0..50, max >= min) which live in openmw_edit_effect.layout
and are never adjusted at runtime.

Validation and result text is routed to the bottom screen in DS mode only
(COMPANION_ENCHANTING_MSG, same shape as COMPANION_ALCHEMY_MSG) because the native transient message
box renders bottom-centre of the TOP screen, behind the DS panels. Same GMSTs, same order, same
sounds — only the delivery changes. There is deliberately no separate "validate without committing"
path: CMP:enchant_buy calls the real onBuyButtonClicked.

Kotlin side: LogParser prefixes -> EnchantSession in GameStateRepository -> EnchantingOverlay
(bottom) and EnchantingTopOverlay (top). Added Aug 20 2026.

